Id: cont001w
Severity: WARN
Category: containers
Check: check_containers
Fix: gpasswd -d USER docker for all but those who would be given root, or go rootless.
References: https://docs.docker.com/engine/security/#docker-daemon-attack-surface
Controls: CIS 4.1, 5.4; NIST AC-6, CM-7; ISO 8.2, 8.9; CE Secure configuration, User access control

The users named may use the Docker (or Podman) socket, through the
group that owns it, usually docker. That is root in all but name: any
of them can run 'docker run -v /:/host --privileged ...' and do what
they like to the host, without a password and without sudo's log. The
socket's group is given to developers for convenience, and whoever
takes over one of their sessions inherits it.

To fix it, keep the group to the people who would be given root anyway
('gpasswd -d USER docker' for the others), or use rootless Docker or
Podman, where each user's containers run as that user and give no more
than they already have. If a member is meant to have it, accept the
finding with tigris-accept.
